{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Linter/Basic.html#Batteries.Tactic.Lint.seesBodiesOf\"><span class=\"name\">Batteries</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">Lint</span>.<span class=\"name\">seesBodiesOf</span></a> </span><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">env</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Environment.html#Lean.Environment\">Lean.Environment</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">i </span><span class=\"fn\">j</span> : <a href=\"./Lean/Environment.html#Lean.ModuleIdx\">Lean.ModuleIdx</a>)</span></span> <span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Bool\">Bool</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"**Alias** of `Batteries.Linter.seesBodiesOf`.\n\n---\n\nWhether elaborating the imported module `i` could see the bodies of the definitions of the\nimported module `j`: `i` is `j`, or is not a `module` file, or reaches `j` through a chain of\n`import all`s. This is when core reserves the equation lemma names of `j`'s definitions in `i`.","docLink":"./Batteries/Linter/Basic.html#Batteries.Tactic.Lint.seesBodiesOf","kind":"def","line":297,"name":"Batteries.Tactic.Lint.seesBodiesOf","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover-community/batteries/blob/dd0900df51045e7d9be143ed167c9d200bcf2b45/Batteries/Linter/Basic.lean#L297-L298"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span><span class=\"decl_name\"> <a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Batteries/Linter/Basic.html#Batteries.Tactic.Lint.shouldBeLinted\"><span class=\"name\">Batteries</span>.<span class=\"name\">Tactic</span>.<span class=\"name\">Lint</span>.<span class=\"name\">shouldBeLinted</span></a> </span><span class=\"impl_arg\"><span class=\"decl_args\"><span class=\"fn\">{<span class=\"fn\">m</span> : <span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./fou